@@ -135,9 +138,11 @@ The translated image is the game's code as LLVM modules and native objects. It i
 
 1. Make the unpacked executable. See [Make the unpacked executable](#make-the-unpacked-executable).
 
-2. Make the function map with Ghidra.
+2. Make the function map with Ghidra. The script reads the function names in the SA2 Mod Loader's `SA2Functions.h`, so first check out the Mod Loader at the commit `tools/pins.json` pins under `sa2-mod-loader`.
 
    ```bash
+   git clone https://github.com/X-Hax/sa2-mod-loader private/predecessor-tools/sa2-mod-loader
+   git -C private/predecessor-tools/sa2-mod-loader checkout 611d686f123e39ee843acea5ceb8d0561233ffea
    .venv/bin/python Documentation/scripts/s1_function_map.py
    ```
 
@@ -170,6 +175,15 @@ Before you assemble a desktop build from a fresh image, generate the tables the
 
 The last command writes the read-set that `tools/s7/release_build.py` checks the unpacked executable against. It needs no recorded game runs, and it writes nothing unless its result matches the hash in `Documentation/receipts/s7-drm-unwrap-v1.json`.
 
+A desktop build links the double f80 mode by default, from objects that `tools/s8/perf_f80.py` compiles from the translated image. Build them for Linux before you run `tools/s7/release_build.py`:
+
+```bash
+source tools/env.sh
+.venv/bin/python tools/s8/perf_f80.py build --target x86_64-linux-musl --mode double --out private/generated/s8/pc-double/linux-obj --jobs 16
+```
+
+The module documentation of `tools/s7/release_build.py` describes the f80 modes and the Windows objects' folder.
+
 Local builds embed the absolute paths of their source files, which can include your user name. Before you share a build, list your home folder and anything else private in a JSON file such as `{"terms": ["/home/yourname"]}`, then check the package:
 
